# Runtime state lives OUTSIDE this directory: <HERMES_HOME>/qdrant.json
# (save_config — may carry a Qdrant API key) and <HERMES_HOME>/qdrant-status.json
# (get_status_config bookkeeping). Writing here would change a file
# pm.workspace.members_stamp() hashes into the venv dependency stamp, re-syncing
# dependencies on every `hermes` launch. These entries only guard against a
# stale copy still writing the old location.
config.json
status.json

# Python / tooling. The two tool caches churn on every run, and
# pm.workspace.members_stamp() hashes them until the core-side fix lands; both
# also ship their own `*` .gitignore, which is what that fix keys on. Declared
# here too so the intent is visible at the root.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
